# Intent: The clock page gets three styles that a tap cycles, and shows when the unit sleeps (owner idea 2026-11-18, spec docs/design/clock-styles.md). Style 0 is the classic big digits on the black card, 1 the ring, 2 date and time (smaller digits and the full date line in the 20 px body text); a tap on the page moves to the next style and back to the first; a sleeping unit shows a moon with "Zz", the page dimmed to 40 percent and a steady colon, and a tap then only wakes the screen and changes nothing. The host interface gains clock_style(), clock_set_style(int) and asleep() with safe defaults; the unit's implementation (saving the style only on change, after a short wait, never from the display task) is the firmware track's, per the spec. Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages.h, maipai_pages_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: the clock page opens in the saved style; a tap shows the next style (classic, ring, date and time, classic); the style is still the same after a restart; when the unit sleeps the page is dim with a moon and Zz and the colon stops blinking; a tap on a sleeping unit wakes it and leaves the style alone.
# Kconfig: none

